For now, the organization remains confined to Heartland, but its presence is felt everywhere. Local party members whisper that their phones are tapped, and troublesome politicians vanish—never to be seen again. With the police now firmly under government control, they decide which crimes to overlook and coordinate raids hand-in-hand with the Commonwealth Army.

Yet, their reach still depends on the willingness of people to betray their comrades by reporting them to the police.